    "A blocked result cannot be completed." : {

    },
    "A briefing is a path through the case for a handover or a review. Its steps point at the case's own records, branches and saved views — nothing is copied. A live briefing shows what changed since each step was added; a frozen one keeps every step as it was when frozen." : {
      "comment" : "A description of a briefing.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A claim adverse to someone named is owed a right of reply even when it is verified. Decide for every claim." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the right of reply for claims that are adverse to someone named.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A clean, plain-language summary you can hand to a non-technical reader — counsel, a manager. Copy or print it." : {

    },
    "A complete, append-only record of what happened to your data — every file acquisition and integrity check, and every human decision. Nothing here is editable or deletable; it is the receipt for the ledger." : {

    },
    "A confirmed statement is never edited. If the interviewee corrects it, record the correction here; it is kept with the statement, in order." : {

    },
    "A corrections path exists after publishing (pinned comment / description edit / erratum)" : {

    },
    "A corrections path exists post-publication" : {

    },
    "A deviation resolves the rule as an authorized departure and downgrades the sealed status to 'conformant with deviations'. Prohibitions are non-waivable — a deviation on one fails the run. Every departure stays on the certificate with who authorized it and why." : {

    },
    "A document in the case. Its presence does not establish that what it says is true." : {
      "comment" : "A description of a document in the case.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A document not read here was not searched, quoted or sent to an AI. Sources ▸ Needs attention can read some of them again." : {
      "comment" : "A description of a document that was not read by the app.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A fact confirmed a year ago may no longer hold. Flagging the oldest confirmations keeps them from being reused as if freshly checked — the difference between a current answer and a confidently wrong one." : {

    },
    "A finding can be right on the evidence yet fail if the process was unfair — confirm both fairness steps." : {

    },
    "A focused, evidence-cited history of one subject — resolved to a canonical identity." : {

    },
    "A folder anyone can verify without Investigations Made Easy — integrity, authenticity and conformance replay (spec: BUNDLE_FORMAT.md; CLI: kalverify)." : {

    },
    "A hold covers the documents in the chosen matter's scope that carry the tag below (and any coded Responsive, Hot or Privileged there). Documents outside the matter are never held by it." : {
      "comment" : "A description of what a legal hold is.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A large email dump, made navigable — exact duplicates removed and scattered replies grouped into conversations, most-recently-active first." : {

    },
    "A link records a stated connection. It does not show that one thing caused another, or that anyone did wrong." : {

    },
    "A link records your reasoning. It is not evidence, and it decides nothing." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the link's purpose.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A linked document is checked against the case's scope. Linking never marks the request fulfilled." : {

    },
    "A live search runs again on the case's documents as they are then; “Check for new matches” lists what is new and adds no document to the case. A frozen result stays as it was." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the difference between a live search and a frozen result.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A matter is the container all jobs run against (a case, story, research question, or personal topic). Name it, pick the workspace holding its documents, and start." : {

    },
    "A one-shot file converter — nothing here is saved to your knowledge base. Reads PDF, Word, Excel, images (OCR), email/PST/NSF, and audio & video (transcribed); exports to text, Markdown, JSON, HTML, CSV, PDF, RTF, Word, Excel, or PNG." : {

    },
    "A one-time App Store purchase. Credit packs never expire; they are spent after the month's credits while an AI plan is active, and stay with your Apple account on every Mac." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the benefits of purchasing a credit pack.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A patent number, a person, a company, a project. The app gathers everything it extracted about it into one cited, chronological file — overview, parties, timeline, clauses, roadblocks, and what's still missing." : {

    },
    "A person verified this entry, but it has changed since (or the result it came from was superseded). Check it again." : {
      "comment" : "A tooltip for the \"A person verified this entry, but it has changed since (or the result it came from was superseded). Check it again.\"",
