    },
    "These are provenance signals, not a verdict. A clean metadata trail is not proof a file is genuine, and a warning is not proof it's fake — it's a lead to investigate. Pixel-level manipulation and AI-generation detection are deliberately out of scope: doing them honestly needs tooling this on-device app doesn't ship, and a false green light would be worse than none." : {

    },
    "These figures assume a %@ — NOT your Mac. After your first LLM-heavy ingest they self-calibrate to this Mac." : {

    },
    "These files are in the archive but hold no readable text, so no answer, job or report draws on them. Press Read again (text recognition can fail while the Mac is busy), Read with AI (Online mode: the pages are read by your Online AI and added as a marked transcription), re-scan with text (OCR), supply a readable copy, or record that the original is unreadable." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the reasons why a file is not readable.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "These files contain app timing and crash stacks: how long the app took to start and respond, memory, CPU and disk counters, and the app's own call stacks at a crash or hang, with the Mac model and macOS and app versions. They contain no documents, no questions or answers, and nothing from your ledger. They were made by macOS on this Mac and have not been sent anywhere." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the contents of the files that will be attached to the email.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "These loaders read external chat + browser data that requires explicit user authorization. Off by default. **App Store**: the sandbox enforces this regardless of toggle." : {

    },
    "These pages were scanned images; the text was recovered by optical character recognition and may be incomplete or imperfect." : {

    },
    "These rows restate source values, so one decision over the rows shown is safe; each row still records its own decision." : {
      "comment" : "A button that accepts all the rows shown in the table.",
